-- title:
--   Uniqueness of the cyclic subgroup cut out by a Γ₀(p^k)-kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field with decidable equality, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $F$ that is elliptic, $p$ a prime and $k$ a natural number, and assume $p \neq 0$ in $F$. Let $h \in F[X]$ satisfy [`ModularCurve.IsGamma0PowAt W p k h`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma0Pow.html#L55), that is: if $p^k = 2$, then $h$ has degree at most $1$ with $h$'s coefficient in degree $1$ equal to $1$ and $h \mid W.\Psi_2^{\mathrm{Sq}}$; and otherwise $h$ has degree at most $\varphi(p^k)/2$ with coefficient $1$ in degree $\varphi(p^k)/2$, the product $h \cdot W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi(p^{k-1})$ divides $W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi(p^k)$, and for every natural number $a$ with $2 \le a \le (p^k-1)/2$ and $p \nmid a$ one has $h \mid W.\mathrm{smulNumerator}\, a\, (\varphi(p^k)/2)\, h$. Let $(x_1,y_1)$ and $(x_2,y_2)$ be nonsingular points of the affine equation of $W$, both of exact additive order $p^k$ in the group of affine points, and suppose $h(x_1) = 0$ and $h(x_2) = 0$. Then the cyclic subgroups generated by the two points coincide: $\mathbb{Z}\cdot(x_1,y_1) = \mathbb{Z}\cdot(x_2,y_2)$ as additive subgroups of the point group of $W$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the dictionary between $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-structures given by kernel polynomials and cyclic subgroups of order $p^k$: a single polynomial satisfying the kernel conditions cuts out the abscissae of the generators of exactly one cyclic subgroup. It is used to show that a $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-structure over an algebraically closed field arises from a unique cyclic subgroup, and in the construction of moduli points for rigidified data of $p$-power level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IsGamma0PowAt_zmultiples_eq_zmultiples_of_isRoot_of_addOrderOf_eq.lean

